  "title": "A two-step bound for the modes of uniform hypercomb summands",
  "batch_label": "primary-20260914",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For every pair of integers n>=2 and ell>=3, let a=(1+(ell-2)x)(1+(ell-1)x), b=x(1+(ell-1)x), z0=1+ell*x, z1=(1+(ell-1)x)(a+2*x), F0=0, F1=1, and Fj=a*F_(j-1)+b*F_(j-2) for j>=2. Set Wn=z1*Fn and Yn=z0*b*F_(n-1), the Galvin-Sharpe Section 2.5 decomposition Cn=Wn+Yn. With zero-extended coefficients define P<=_lr Q by p_i*q_j>=p_j*q_i for all integers i<j. Then Wn<=_lr x^2*Yn and Yn<=_lr x*Wn. Hence the smallest coefficient-maximizing indices satisfy m(Yn)-1<=m(Wn)<=m(Yn)+2. In particular, Cn is nondecreasing up to r=min(m(Wn),m(Yn)) and nonincreasing from q=max(m(Wn),m(Yn)), where q-r<=2. The summand separation bound two is attained by unique modes 6 and 4 at n=3,ell=5. Full unimodality and log-concavity of Cn for all parameters remain unproved here.",
